# Vendor Analysis File Structure

When generating or revising evaluation content for SOW sections (e.g. `4.9.1`, `4.9.2`, etc.):

- **Eval logs (researched documents):** `Glean/Combined/4.9.<N> <Section Name>/<Field Name>.md` - one folder per SOW section, one file per field.
  - Example: `Glean/Combined/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/Features Confirmed.md`, `Glean/Combined/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/Features Not Confirmed.md`
  - No dash between `4.9.<N>` and the section name in the folder; no `Field N` prefix or version suffix (`-2.0`, etc.) in the filename - use git history for versioning.
  - Each section folder gets an `Overview.md` carrying the shared header (Category, Vendor, Evaluator, Visibility Tier, Evaluation Date, Overall Section Status, tenant test stack, companion runbook link) plus a list linking every field file in the folder.
  - `Glean/` root (outside `Combined/`) is for raw/loose research inputs only (`Glean/<vendor>/cloude/` sources, sitemaps, source docx exports) - never place a finalized per-field eval doc there.
- **Test guides:** `test/Glean/4.9.<N> <Section Name>/<Field Name>.md` - same folder-per-section, file-per-field pattern, filenames matching the paired eval-log field names 1:1.
  - Example: `test/Glean/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/Features Confirmed.md`, `test/Glean/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/Features Not Confirmed.md`
  - Each section folder gets a `Pre-Flight.md` carrying shared setup (purpose, tenant entry, identities, content pack) plus any cross-field reference material (schedule, evidence mapping, cheat sheet, safety rules).
- **Deep-dive / re-verified research (V2):** a deeper re-verification pass on a field lives in a `V2/` subfolder inside that section folder, filename matching the original field name exactly - e.g. `Glean/Combined/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/V2/Features Confirmed.md` and `test/Glean/4.9.1 Functional Capabilities/V2/Features Confirmed.md`. The base field file links to it via "**Deep dive (V2):**"; the V2 file links back to the base field file. Do one field's V2 pass, get it verified, before starting the next field's V2 pass.
- **Cross-linking:** every field file links to its folder's `Overview.md`/`Pre-Flight.md` and to its paired file on the other side (eval ↔ test guide).
- Sourcing rule (`vendor-analysis-web-sourcing.mdc`) still applies inside every one of these files.
